----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let a = 1000

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let d = 0

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let q = 10 /! d
let a2 = a

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let e = a + 1

----------
expect all four units are entered, and unit 3 returns early before its take
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `a` = 1000 |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | `d` = 0 |
| 3 | takes `a` (1), reads `d` (2) | compiles, returns early | `10 /! 0` | - |
| 4 | reads `a` (1) | compile fails | `a` is given away by unit 3 | - |

----------
scriptunit-edit 2
----------

let d = 5

----------
expect unit 2 is edited so unit 3 finishes
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | unit 3 returned early before taking `a`, so `a` is as unit 1 made it | `a` moved |
| 2 | - | recompiles, runs | edited | `d` = 5 |
| 3 | takes `a` (1), reads `d` (2) | reruns | reads `d` from unit 2 | `q` = 2, `a2` = 1000 |
| 4 | reads `a` (1) | untouched | still cannot name `a` | - |

----------
engine
----------

| unit | this step | note |
|------|-----------|------|
| 1 | reruns | assumes a unit that returned early did everything its code could, so reruns unit 1 for a take that never happened |

